From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Toon Verwaest <verwaest@chromium.org>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 11:07:05 +0200
Subject: [maglev] Mark sloppy eval context extension slot as mutable
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

In MaglevReducer::GetContextMaybeAssigned, header slots up to
scope_info.ContextHeaderLength() were unconditionally marked as
kNotAssigned (with VariableMode::kConst). When HasContextExtensionSlot()
is true, Context::EXTENSION_INDEX (slot 2) falls within
ContextHeaderLength().

For scopes where SloppyEvalCanExtendVars() is true, the context
extension slot is initialized to undefined and can be mutated at runtime
when sloppy eval declares variables. Treating it as kNotAssigned caused
TrySpecializeLoadContextSlotToFunctionContext to constant-fold the
extension slot in CheckContextExtensions to undefined, and cached loads
in loaded_context_constants_ across calls.

Return kMaybeAssigned (with VariableMode::kVar) for
Context::EXTENSION_INDEX when scope_info.SloppyEvalCanExtendVars() is
true.

TAG=agy
CONV=1b7d9654-2731-4157-8abc-cd9414138332

Bug: 559932543
Change-Id: I2ae18d66e935ac13dd0f361bf2aab7c37527e95c
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/v8/v8/+/8420505
Reviewed-by: Marja Hölttä <marja@chromium.org>
